{% from "govuk/components/details/macro.njk" import govukDetails %}

{{ govukDetails({
    summaryText: "How to use the Suggested Case Notes",
    html: '
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-top-6">How the AI tool works</h2>
    <p>The AI tool searches case notes recorded in DPS during the previous 90 days. It uses search criteria developed with the National Safety Team to identify case notes containing information that may be relevant to understanding:</p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>recent incidents and patterns of behaviour</li>
        <li>possible risks and triggers</li>
        <li>protective factors that may reduce risk or support positive behaviour</li>
        <li>relevant background information and context</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The tool highlights extracts from suggested case notes and lets you view each full note as it was written, so you can check the context.</p>
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-top-6">What you need to do</h2>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Review the suggested case notes, focusing on those you judge most relevant.</li>
        <li>Use your professional judgement to decide what information is relevant to this part of the investigation.</li>
        <li>Summarise key information in your own words. Copying and pasting whole case notes is unlikely to be helpful, though specific extracts may be useful where appropriate.</li>
        <li>The suggested case notes are one source of information to consider. Also speak with the prisoner and consider their views, speak with relevant staff who know or support them, and review other relevant sources, including OASys, DPS Alerts, the Safety Diagnostic Tool, other DPS information, and historical case notes.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-top-6">Important to know</h2>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>The AI tool helps you find information. It does not make decisions for you.</li>
        <li>The tool may make mistakes. If you know of a relevant case note that is missing, you should still include that information in your investigation.</li>
        <li>The tool does not rewrite or summarise case notes; it presents them as they were written.</li>
        <li>You remain responsible for reviewing and acting on the information.</li>
        <li>The tool is designed to be safe and transparent, and aligned with the MOJ’s AI policy.</li>
    </ul>'
}) }}
